(a) The following days are declared legal holidays for the employees of the city:
(1) New Year's Day;
(2) Martin Luther King Jr. Day;
(3) Memorial Day;
(4) Juneteenth National Independence Day;
(5) Independence Day;
(6) Labor Day;
(7) Thanksgiving Day and the day after Thanksgiving;
(8) Christmas Eve (if Christmas Eve falls on Friday, Saturday, or Sunday, holiday will be observed on Friday); and
(9) Christmas Day (if Christmas Day falls on a Saturday or Sunday, holiday will be observed on Monday).
(b) If a legal holiday falls on Saturday, the Friday preceding the holiday shall be the legal holiday. If a legal holiday falls on Sunday, the Monday following the holiday shall be the legal holiday.
(c) City hall will be closed for regular business on legal holidays.
(Code 2001, § 2-3-2; Ord. No. 106-03, 12-8-2003; Ord. No. 148-04, 11-8-2004; Ord. No. 2024-634, § 1, 8-12-2024)

